Subject: win32u: Read the screen from the desktop share

BitBlt and StretchBlt from the screen (GetDC(NULL), the desktop window,
a DISPLAY DC) only saw Wine's own windows: the X server under a Wayland
session holds nothing else. The source is now a bitmap filled from the
portal streams, once the user has shared the screens. Reads smaller than
a quarter of a screen never open the picker, and neither does a read the
user did not ask for: the picker comes after a click, a key or a
hotkey of the program, or when it keeps reading like a recorder (libraye-capture's
rcap_gdi_read_asks decides). RAYE_SCREEN_CAPTURE_GDI=0 turns it off.
